// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 22-surface-syntax
// facility: spec/22 §1 byte-char-literal (lexical ill-formedness); D-0033
// kind: negative
// expect: parse-error
//
// A `byte-char-literal`'s character must be ASCII: `é` is two bytes
// in UTF-8, not one. `b'\xe9'` writes the byte 0xE9.

fn main()
{
    u8 c = b'é';
}
